  "question": {
    "text": "Let the tangent to the parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be perpendicular to the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Then the square of distance of the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from the normal to the hyperbola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;at its point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to .............",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "116",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>The tangent to the parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be perpendicular to the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So, Slope of tangent&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br />So, equation of hyperbola will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>324</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />Now equation of tangent at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>y</mi></mrow><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math><br />So, slope of normal<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math><br />Now finding, equation of normal&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Now finding,distance from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>29</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>58</mn><msqrt><mn>29</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>29</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>29</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>116</mn></math></p>",
